proach would be to use a single `with self._heap_lock:` block around the entire stopping logic to ensure that all operations on the heap and job states are atomic with respect to the stop event. This will make it more likely that all worker threads will exit promptly upon receiving the stop signal.\n\n6. If a job's `fn` raises and `attempts == max_attempts`, the final value of `job.state` is `JobState.DEAD`. The metrics counter incremented in this scenario is \"dead\".",
